github_url: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/issues/100"
body: "The replay adapter bypasses the `ambiguous_model` refusal added in PR #99. Against the same conflicting native inventory, direct admission refuses while replay selects whichever equivalent reference appears first and submits inference. Verified on `93c51cb0d51b20b33fcd38dbf76a22bbcdc093f0` with the built package and a synthetic loopback HTTP endpoint; no model or hosted service was used.\n\n### Exact source\n\n- [Replay picks the first normalized reference and immediately pins its digest](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/93c51cb0d51b20b33fcd38dbf76a22bbcdc093f0/policy-replay.ts#L219-L229).\n- [Admission only checks conflicting normalized references when the input is not already digest-addressed](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/93c51cb0d51b20b33fcd38dbf76a22bbcdc093f0/decision-admission.ts#L149-L163). Passing the replay-selected digest makes this gate unreachable for replay.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nNode 24.19.0 and lockfile dependencies. The committed `admissionMetadata` helper supplies the pinned template and a small supported byte vocabulary. The loopback server records real requests from the TypeSafe SDK. The second replay reverses only the inventory order.\n\n```sh\nwork=$(mktemp -d)\ngit clone --quiet https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev.git \"$work/package\"\ncd \"$work/package\"\ngit checkout --quiet 93c51cb0d51b20b33fcd38dbf76a22bbcdc093f0\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund\nnpm run build\ncat > repro.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport {createServer} from 'node:http';\nimport {admitDecision, createOllamaReplayAdapter} from './dist/index.js';\nimport {admissionMetadata} from './test/admission-fixtures.ts';\nconst requests=[];\nlet models=[{name:'tev1:4b',digest:'a'.repeat(64),capabilities:['decision']},{name:'registry.ollama.ai/library/tev1:4b',digest:'b'.repeat(64),capabilities:['decision']}];\nconst server=createServer(async(req,res)=>{let text='';for await(const chunk of req)text+=chunk;const body=text?JSON.parse(text):{};requests.push({path:req.url,model:body.model});res.setHeader('content-type','application/json');res.end(JSON.stringify(req.url==='/api/tags'?{models}:req.url==='/api/show'?admissionMetadata():{model:body.model,answers:{keep:{type:'noul',noul:0.9}},usage:{input_tokens:1,output_tokens:1}}));});\nawait new Promise(r=>server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',r));\ntry{const baseUrl=`http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`;\nconst config={provider:'ollama',baseUrl,model:'tev1:4b',timeoutMs:10000,totalDeadlineMs:10000};\nconst questions={keep:{type:'noul'}};\ntry{await admitDecision(config,'fixture',questions);}catch(e){console.log('direct admission:',e.code);}\nfor(let i=0;i<2;i++){const adapter=await createOllamaReplayAdapter('tev1:4b',baseUrl);const result=await adapter.decide({id:'fixture',state:'fixture',questions,result:{},policy:{version:'v1',min_probability:0.5}});\nconsole.log('replay selected digest:',result.model.slice(7,15));models.reverse();}\nconsole.log('inference requests:',requests.filter(r=>r.path==='/v1/systemone').length);\n}finally{server.closeAllConnections();await new Promise(r=>server.close(r));}\nEOF\nPM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_AGENT_PROBES=0 NODE_ENV=test node repro.mjs\n```\n\nObserved output:\n\n```text\ndirect admission: ambiguous_model\nreplay selected digest: aaaaaaaa\nreplay selected digest: bbbbbbbb\ninference requests: 2\n```\n\n### Expected / actual\n\nExpected: conflicting digests for equivalent native model names refuse before `/api/show` or inference, including through `createOllamaReplayAdapter`. The refusal should explain how to resolve the inventory conflict or explicitly select a verified digest.\n\nActual: direct admission reports `ambiguous_model`, but both replay calls succeed and choose different model digests solely because the inventory order changes. Two inference requests are submitted.\n\n### Impact and fix direction\n\nReplay can evaluate a recording against an arbitrary member of a conflicting model identity, making results order-dependent despite the shared admission contract. Digest pinning protects the choice after selection but does not establish that the alias was unambiguous.\n\nShare one validated native-reference resolver across admission and replay, check all equivalent inventory rows before selecting a digest, and retain the replay path's local/non-cloud restrictions. Cover both inventory orders and same-digest duplicate spellings with actual request-count assertions.\n\nDuplicate check: searched all issue states for `replay ambiguous` and inspected the issue inventory. Closed issue #93 concerns equivalent-name rejection; this is a distinct surviving replay bypass of the conflict refusal introduced by its follow-up.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-06T11:02:32Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-jev#99 - Fix Tev1 admission references, Unicode regressions and smoke cleanup [closed]\n> unbraind/pm-jev#92 - Reject local decisions that exceed the pinned model context [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
